  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1015 PM CDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nThe upper ridge centered just to our west appears to become \nbetter amplified toward the later half of the week keeping above \nnormal temperatures in place across the Great Plains and much of \nthe Southeast. High pressure and large scale subsidence will \ncontinue to promote dry weather so much so that even cloud cover \nwill be hard to come by until at least late in the weekend. Highs \nwill reach the mid to upper 70s each afternoon, perhaps even \nreaching the 80 degree mark in some locations. Clear skies and \ncalm overnight conditions will allow for good diurnal cooling, \nwith lows in the 40s each night. Long term guidance becomes a bit \nmore unclear regarding the upper level pattern toward the end of \nthe weekend, so we will continue to focus on the above-normal \ndaytime temperatures while we monitor trends for any potential \nfronts early next week.",
